# 0023 core: i915 owns the eDP pipe -- K2 boot commit, K3 modesets, J1 joiner, Tile4 plane, C1 cursor, K4 boot mode
#
# Base:  the core after 0022
# Files: gpu/xegfx/shim/src/xnu/xg_kext.cpp, gpu/xegfx/shim/include/xg_i915.h,
#        gpu/xkpi/src/i915/xg_display_hook.c/.h, gpu/xkpi/src/i915/intel_display_driver.c,
#        gpu/xkpi/src/i915/intel_modeset_setup.c, gpu/xkpi/src/i915/xg_i915_exec.c, gpu/xkpi/exclude.txt,
#        gpu/xkpi/src/i915/i915_gem_execbuffer.c (new overlay; the full file, derived from drm-kmod's i915_gem_execbuffer.c)
# Apply: patch -p1 < patches/0023-core-kms-boot-commit-joiner-cursor.patch
#
# Why: scaled HiDPI and 240/300 Hz need i915 to program the panel (HBR3 + DSC, the plane scaler, the pipe joiner);
# the firmware raster kept by K1 is 60 Hz at the native size only.  NVRAM xegfx-disp-kms picks the stage:
#   K2a (2)  atomic checks only (drm_atomic_check_only) of the read-out state and of the adapter's scanout geometry
#   K2  (3)  one boot commit through i915 (DRRS off, 8 bpc, PSR off) with a placeholder framebuffer on the primary
#            plane; the fixed modes are captured for the adapter afterwards
#   K3       KAPI v1 additions: getTiming(XG_KMS_FIXED_MODE_BASE + n) returns fixed mode n, setMode(ctx, 0, n) commits
#            it; a plane-only commit takes a new desktop size (the scaler maps it onto the raster)
#   J1       when one pipe cannot carry the plane (3840x2400 at 240/300 Hz) pipe A is joined with pipe B;
#            "xgJoinerInfo" tells the accel where pipe B's plane points so its PLANE_SURF follows every flip
#   Tile4    xg_display_kms_plane_layout() re-commits the placeholder with the Tile4 modifier (plane only), so
#            WindowServer's Tile4 frames are scanned correctly; DPT is off (enable_dpt=0)
#   C1       hardware cursor: one commit puts i915's cursor plane on the joiner seam, then CUR_POS/CUR_CTL/CUR_BASE
#            are written per pipe by KAPI reserved[6] cursorImage / reserved[7] cursorMove (image pre-scaled to the
#            raster); every commit re-applies them
#   K4       boot mode: NVRAM xegfx-disp-bootmode ('XBM1', refresh mHz, desktop w, h; written by the adapter) makes
#            the boot commit run that fixed mode and desktop (joined when needed) instead of the 60 Hz preferred mode;
#            getTiming(XG_KMS_BOOT_STATE_INDEX) reports it so the adapter adopts it without a modeset.  A refused mode
#            falls back to the K2 commit.
# Also: backlight and vblank-wait KAPI calls, GPU clock read-out / minimum-frequency pin (xg_i915_gt_text, debug
# sysctls) and per-stage execbuffer timing (debug.xegfx_eb).  Without the NVRAM keys behaviour is that of 0022.
# Status: in daily use on ARL-HX (Xe-LPG): boots straight into 1920x1200 HiDPI at 240 Hz (3840x2400, joined).
#
