+/*
+ * GPU clock (native-display docs/32-FRAME-RATE.md §32.13): Dock and Genie animations run 20-50 fps with the flip worker
+ * waiting 8-67 ms for each composite, while the same desktop does 100+ fps once the animation is over.  Linux boosts the
+ * clock when a client waits for its work; WindowServer no longer waits (E1) and the flip worker only polls, so these
+ * report the clock and let it be pinned up from the minimum.  Thread context.
+ */
+int
+xg_i915_gt_text(char *out, int max)
